  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "concept": "define corrosion",
      "narration": "Corrosion is a natural process where materials, especially metals, degrade due to chemical or electrochemical reactions with their environment. Examples include rusting of iron, tarnishing of silver, and patina on copper. This degradation happens when metals interact with water, oxygen, or moisture in the air.",
