    {
      "id": "s5",
      "concept": "pitting corrosion",
      "narration": "Pitting corrosion happens when a small particle like dust or water droplet traps low oxygen on a metal surface. This creates an anode with low oxygen and a cathode with high oxygen, forming an electrochemical cell that drives localized corrosion.",
