      "id": "s6",
      "concept": "galvanic corrosion",
      "narration": "When two dissimilar metals touch in a wet environment, the one with lower electrode potential (more negative) becomes the anode and corrodes. Iron (-0.44V) corrodes when connected to copper (+0.34V), while copper is protected.",
